      "traceTextDiagram": "CAS Store Factory \u0026 Configuration Loading\n├── Agent Daemon Initialization\n│   └── OpenCASStore callback \u003c-- 1a\n│       └── cas.OpenDefault() \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/factory.go:51\n│           ├── LoadConfig(rootDir) \u003c-- 1b\n│           │   ├── Read AGENTCTL_CAS_DRIVER env \u003c-- 1c\n│           │   ├── loadSQLiteConfig() (default) \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/config.go:163\n│           │   └── Return Config struct \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/config.go:220\n│           └── OpenCAS(ctx, cfg) \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/factory.go:14\n│               ├── cfg.Validate() \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/factory.go:15\n│               ├── Driver switch statement \u003c-- 1d\n│               │   ├── DriverFile → NewStore() \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/factory.go:24\n│               │   ├── DriverSQLite → NewSQLiteStore() \u003c-- 1e\n│               │   └── DriverTurso → NewTursoStore() \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/factory.go:28\n│               └── autoMigrate() check \u003c-- 1f\n                    └── MigrateFromFile() if needed \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/migrate.go:148",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nAgentctl needs to store large outputs (logs, results, artifacts) without bloating envelopes or overwhelming context windows. The **CAS (Content-Addressable Storage) system** solves this by storing content once by its SHA256 digest and returning a reference. The system supports **three storage backends**: legacy file-based storage, SQLite for local databases, and Turso for cloud-replicated storage. Users can switch backends via environment variables without code changes.\n\n## Details\n\n### Factory Pattern and Configuration\n\nThe entry point is `cas.OpenDefault()` [1a], which loads configuration from environment variables [1b]. The **AGENTCTL_CAS_DRIVER** environment variable determines the backend [1c]: `file` for legacy filesystem storage, `sqlite` for local database (default), or `turso` for cloud storage. The factory pattern [1d] switches on the driver type and instantiates the appropriate store implementation [1e].\n\n### Backend Selection\n\n- **File-based**: Legacy implementation storing content in `~/.agentctl/cas/sha256/\u003chex\u003e` with `.json` metadata files\n- **SQLite**: Default backend storing blobs directly in a database table with 1MB inline threshold\n- **Turso**: Cloud-replicated libsql with embedded replica for offline-first operation\n\n### Auto-Migration\n\nWhen switching from file-based to database backends, the system automatically detects legacy CAS directories and migrates objects on first access [1f]. Migration is incremental—only new objects not yet in the destination are copied. This ensures zero-downtime transitions between storage backends.\n\n### Configuration Hierarchy\n\nConfiguration follows a three-layer hierarchy:\n1. **Defaults**: SQLite driver, 1MB blob threshold, WAL mode enabled\n2. **Config file**: `~/.agentctl/config.yaml` settings\n3. **Environment variables**: `AGENTCTL_CAS_*` vars override everything\n\nThe `LoadConfig()` function [1b] merges these layers, with environment variables taking precedence for operational flexibility in different deployment contexts."
    },
