      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Auto-Migration from Legacy File Store\n├── Factory triggers migration check\n│   └── autoMigrate() called after store open \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/factory.go:40\n│       ├── Check source directory exists \u003c-- 5a\n│       ├── Scan sha256/ for content files \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/migrate.go:89\n│       ├── Filter: only files with .json \u003c-- 5b\n│       ├── Build destination digest set \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/migrate.go:124\n│       ├── Count pending migrations \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/migrate.go:130\n│       └── Execute migration \u003c-- 5c\n│           └── MigrateFromFile() \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/migrate.go:71\n│               └── Migrate() core logic \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/migrate.go:21\n│                   └── for each object: \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/migrate.go:29\n│                       ├── src.Get() \u003c-- 5d\n│                       ├── dst.Put() \u003c-- 5e\n│                       └── dst.Pin() if pinned \u003c-- 5f\n└── Result: objects copied to new backend",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen agentctl transitions from **legacy file-based CAS storage** to modern **database-backed storage** (SQLite or Turso), existing content-addressed objects need to be preserved. Without auto-migration, users would lose access to previously stored artifacts, breaking references in cached results, pinned outputs, and historical job data. The auto-migration system [5a-5f] solves this by **automatically detecting and copying legacy objects** to the new backend on first access, ensuring zero data loss during the storage backend transition.\n\n## Details\n\n**Migration trigger**: When a CAS store opens with a non-file driver (SQLite/Turso), the factory checks if `AutoMigrate` is enabled and a legacy file store exists [5a]. The system scans the `sha256/` directory for content files that have corresponding `.json` metadata files [5b]—objects without metadata are skipped as they cannot be reliably migrated.\n\n**Incremental migration**: The system builds a set of digests already present in the destination store and counts how many source objects are missing [5b]. Only **new objects are migrated**, making subsequent runs fast. The actual migration [5c] reads each object from the source file store [5d], writes it to the destination database [5e], and preserves the pinned status [5f].\n\n**Safety guarantees**: Migration is **best-effort and non-blocking**—if it fails, the error is logged to stderr but doesn't prevent the store from opening. Objects are copied, not moved, so the legacy file store remains intact as a backup. The migration runs synchronously during store initialization, ensuring all legacy content is available before any new operations begin."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "title": "Database Driver Selection \u0026 Initialization",
      "description": "Database driver layer abstracts SQLite/libsql/Turso backends with unified interface and vector search support",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "6a",
          "path": "internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go",
          "lineNumber": 91,
          "lineContent": "func OpenDB(ctx context.Context, cfg Config, migrate MigrationFunc) (DB, error) {",
          "title": "OpenDB entry point",
          "description": "Unified database opening with driver selection"
        },
        {
          "id": "6b",
          "path": "internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go",
          "lineNumber": 96,
          "lineContent": "switch cfg.Driver {",
          "title": "Driver type switch",
          "description": "Select implementation based on driver config"
        },
        {
          "id": "6c",
          "path": "internal/storage/dbdriver/sqlite.go",
          "lineNumber": 28,
          "lineContent": "db, err := sql.Open(\"sqlite\", cfg.Path)",
          "title": "Open SQLite connection",
          "description": "Standard SQLite driver (no vector search)"
        },
        {
          "id": "6d",
          "path": "internal/storage/dbdriver/libsql.go",
          "lineNumber": 51,
          "lineContent": "connector, err = libsql.NewEmbeddedReplicaConnector(cfg.Path, cfg.SyncURL, opts...)",
          "title": "Create libsql connector",
          "description": "Local libsql with optional remote sync (supports vectors)"
        },
        {
          "id": "6e",
          "path": "internal/storage/dbdriver/turso.go",
          "lineNumber": 56,
          "lineContent": "connector, err := libsql.NewEmbeddedReplicaConnector(dbPath, cfg.URL,\n\t\tlibsql.WithAuthToken(cfg.AuthToken),\n\t)",
          "title": "Create Turso connector",
          "description": "Embedded replica syncing with Turso cloud"
        },
        {
          "id": "6f",
          "path": "internal/storage/dbdriver/turso.go",
          "lineNumber": 96,
          "lineContent": "if err := ensureVectorSupport(ctx, db, vectorDims); err != nil {",
          "title": "Enable vector search",
          "description": "Verify vector functions available in Turso group"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Database Driver Selection \u0026 Initialization\n├── CAS SQLite Store Creation\n│   └── NewSQLiteStore() \u003c-- internal/storage/cas/sqlite_store.go:33\n│       └── dbdriver.OpenDB() \u003c-- 6a\n│           ├── cfg.Validate() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:92\n│           └── switch cfg.Driver \u003c-- 6b\n│               ├── case DriverSQLite \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:97\n│               │   └── openSQLite() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:98\n│               │       └── sql.Open(\"sqlite\") \u003c-- 6c\n│               ├── case DriverLibSQL \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:99\n│               │   └── openLibSQL() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:100\n│               │       ├── libsql.NewEmbedded\n│               │       │   ReplicaConnector() \u003c-- 6d\n│               │       └── sql.OpenDB(connector) \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/libsql.go:64\n│               └── case DriverTurso \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:101\n│                   └── openTurso() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:102\n│                       ├── libsql.NewEmbedded\n│                       │   ReplicaConnector() \u003c-- 6e\n│                       ├── sql.OpenDB(connector) \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/turso.go:68\n│                       └── ensureVectorSupport() \u003c-- 6f",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nagentctl needs to store content-addressable objects (CAS) for large outputs, artifacts, and cached results. The system must support **three different storage backends**: legacy file-based storage, local SQLite databases, and cloud-based Turso databases. Each backend has different characteristics—files are simple but don't scale well, SQLite provides local database features, and Turso enables cloud sync with vector search capabilities. The database driver layer provides a **unified interface** so that higher-level code (like CAS stores) doesn't need to know which backend is being used.\n\n## Details\n\n### Driver Selection\n\nThe `OpenDB` function [6a] is the single entry point for opening any database connection. It validates the configuration and then switches on the driver type [6b] to route to the appropriate implementation. This factory pattern keeps backend selection centralized.\n\n### Three Backend Implementations\n\n**SQLite** [6c] uses the standard `database/sql` driver with no special features—just local file-based storage with WAL mode for concurrency. It's the simplest option with no external dependencies.\n\n**libsql** [6d] creates an embedded replica connector that can optionally sync with a remote sqld server. This enables **local-first operation** with background sync to a remote database. The connector is wrapped with `sql.OpenDB` to provide the standard database interface.\n\n**Turso** [6e] is cloud-based and also uses libsql's embedded replica connector, but always syncs with Turso's cloud infrastructure. It requires authentication tokens and can optionally enable **vector search** [6f] for semantic operations. The `ensureVectorSupport` function verifies that the Turso database group has vector extensions enabled by attempting to create a test table with `F32_BLOB` columns.\n\n### Configuration Flow\n\nThe CAS SQLite store calls `OpenDB` with a `dbdriver.Config` that specifies the driver type and backend-specific settings (paths, URLs, tokens, vector dimensions). Environment variables like `AGENTCTL_CAS_DRIVER` control which backend is selected at runtime, defaulting to SQLite for simplicity."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "title": "Configuration Loading with CAS Policy",
      "description": "Config system loads CAS policy settings (store/expose) from defaults, config file, and environment variables",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "7a",
          "path": "internal/platform/config/config.go",
          "lineNumber": 249,
          "lineContent": "func Load(_ context.Context, opts ...Option) (Config, error) {",
          "title": "Config Load entry",
          "description": "Main configuration loading function"
        },
        {
          "id": "7b",
          "path": "internal/platform/config/config.go",
          "lineNumber": 320,
          "lineContent": "v.SetDefault(\"cas.store\", true)",
          "title": "Default CAS store enabled",
          "description": "By default, always store large outputs in CAS"
        },
        {
          "id": "7c",
          "path": "internal/platform/config/config.go",
          "lineNumber": 321,
          "lineContent": "v.SetDefault(\"cas.expose\", \"off\")",
          "title": "Default expose policy off",
          "description": "By default, hide digests from output (debugging only)"
        },
        {
          "id": "7d",
          "path": "internal/platform/config/config.go",
          "lineNumber": 416,
          "lineContent": "if storeEnv := os.Getenv(\"AGENTCTL_CAS_STORE\"); storeEnv != \"\" {",
          "title": "Override from environment",
          "description": "AGENTCTL_CAS_STORE env var overrides config file"
        },
        {
          "id": "7e",
          "path": "internal/platform/config/config.go",
          "lineNumber": 420,
          "lineContent": "switch strings.ToLower(exposeEnv) {",
          "title": "Parse expose policy",
          "description": "AGENTCTL_CAS_EXPOSE: off/digest/hint"
        },
        {
          "id": "7f",
          "path": "internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/context.go",
          "lineNumber": 86,
          "lineContent": "return !rc.NoCAS \u0026\u0026 rc.Config.CAS.Store",
          "title": "Check if CAS enabled",
          "description": "Skills check policy before storing large outputs"
        },
        {
          "id": "7g",
          "path": "internal/adapters/skillslib/skillout/emit.go",
          "lineNumber": 115,
          "lineContent": "switch expose {",
          "title": "Apply policy in skill output",
          "description": "Skills respect expose policy when building output"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Configuration Loading with CAS Policy\n├── Config.Load() entry point \u003c-- 7a\n│   ├── parseOptions() \u003c-- internal/platform/config/config.go:274\n│   ├── newConfiguredViper() \u003c-- internal/platform/config/config.go:282\n│   │   └── SetEnvPrefix(\"AGENTCTL\") \u003c-- internal/platform/config/config.go:284\n│   ├── applyDefaults() \u003c-- internal/platform/config/config.go:290\n│   │   ├── SetDefault(\"cas.store\", true) \u003c-- 7b\n│   │   └── SetDefault(\"cas.expose\", \"off\") \u003c-- 7c\n│   ├── configureConfigFile() \u003c-- internal/platform/config/config.go:324\n│   ├── readConfig() - read YAML \u003c-- internal/platform/config/config.go:334\n│   ├── decodeConfig() - unmarshal \u003c-- internal/platform/config/config.go:345\n│   └── finalizeConfig() \u003c-- internal/platform/config/config.go:352\n│       ├── Check AGENTCTL_CAS_STORE env \u003c-- 7d\n│       └── Parse AGENTCTL_CAS_EXPOSE \u003c-- 7e\n│\nUsage in Skills\n├── RunContext.ShouldStoreCAS() \u003c-- 7f\n│   └── checks !NoCAS \u0026\u0026 Config.CAS.Store \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/context.go:86\n└── skillout.BuildCASResult() \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillout/emit.go:109\n    └── switch on expose policy \u003c-- 7g\n        ├── ExposePolicyOff → stored:true \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillout/emit.go:118\n        ├── ExposePolicyDigest → artifact \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillout/emit.go:121\n        └── ExposePolicyHint → artifact+hint \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillout/emit.go:125",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nSkills and tools in agentctl can produce arbitrarily large outputs (logs, file contents, analysis results). Sending megabytes of data inline in JSON responses creates two problems: **context window bloat** for LLMs and **slow network transfers**. The CAS (Content-Addressable Storage) policy system solves this by automatically storing large outputs in a digest-addressed store and controlling how those digests appear in responses.\n\nThe key tension: **debugging requires access to full outputs**, but **production workflows need concise responses**. The policy system balances these needs through three modes:\n- **`off`**: Store in CAS but hide digests (debugging only, no user-facing references)\n- **`digest`**: Include raw `sha256:...` digests in output\n- **`hint`**: Include digests plus retrieval commands like `agentctl cas read \u003cdigest\u003e`\n\n## Details\n\n### Configuration Loading\n\nThe system loads CAS policy through a layered approach [7a]: **defaults** → **config file** → **environment variables**. \n\nDefault policy is conservative [7b, 7c]: `cas.store=true` (always persist for debugging) and `cas.expose=off` (hide from output). This means large outputs are captured but not advertised to users by default.\n\nEnvironment variables provide runtime overrides [7d, 7e]: `AGENTCTL_CAS_STORE=true/false` controls storage, while `AGENTCTL_CAS_EXPOSE=off/digest/hint` controls visibility. The config system parses these in `finalizeConfig()` after loading YAML settings, ensuring env vars win.\n\n### Policy Application in Skills\n\nSkills check the policy before truncating outputs [7f]. The `RunContext.ShouldStoreCAS()` method returns `true` only if both conditions hold: CAS is not explicitly disabled (`!NoCAS`) **and** the config enables storage (`Config.CAS.Store`).\n\nWhen building truncated output, `BuildCASResult()` [7g] switches on the expose policy to construct the response payload. The **`off` policy** returns `{\"stored\": true, \"truncated\": true}` with no digest. The **`digest` policy** adds `\"artifact\": \"sha256:...\"`. The **`hint` policy** goes further, embedding a `hint` object with `read_command` and `get_command` fields containing ready-to-run CLI commands [7g].\n\n### Why Three Policies?\n\n- **`off`**: For hooks and internal tools where CAS references would confuse users or leak implementation details\n- **`digest`**: For programmatic consumers that can resolve digests themselves\n- **`hint`**: For interactive AI assistants that benefit from explicit retrieval instructions\n\nThe default `off` policy reflects the design philosophy: **capture everything for debugging, but keep user-facing output clean unless explicitly configured otherwise**."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Maps the content-addressable storage system with three backend implementations (file-based, SQLite, Turso), configuration loading with CAS policy settings, auto-migration from legacy storage, and integration points in daemon and output handling. Key entry points: factory at [1b], file Put at [2b], SQLite Put at [3b], output truncation at [4b], migration at [5b], driver selection at [6b].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph Config[\"Configuration System\"]\n        7a[\"7a: Load config\"]\n        7b[\"7b: Default CAS store=true\"]\n        7c[\"7c: Default expose=off\"]\n        7d[\"7d: Override from env\"]\n        7e[\"7e: Parse expose policy\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Factory[\"Factory \u0026 Orchestration\"]\n        1a[\"1a: OpenDefault entry\"]\n        1b[\"1b: LoadConfig\"]\n        1c[\"1c: Read driver env\"]\n        1d[\"1d: Select backend\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Create store\"]\n        1f[\"1f: Trigger migration\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph FileStore[\"File Store Legacy\"]\n        2a[\"2a: Put entry\"]\n        2b[\"2b: Create temp file\"]\n        2c[\"2c: Compute SHA256\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Generate digest\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Atomic rename\"]\n        2f[\"2f: Write metadata\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph DBAbstraction[\"Database Abstraction Layer\"]\n        6a[\"6a: OpenDB entry\"]\n        6b[\"6b: Driver switch\"]\n        6c[\"6c: Open SQLite\"]\n        6d[\"6d: Create libsql\"]\n        6e[\"6e: Create Turso\"]\n        6f[\"6f: Enable vectors\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph DBStores[\"Database-Backed Stores\"]\n        3a[\"3a: Open SQLite\"]\n        3b[\"3b: Read content\"]\n        3c[\"3c: Compute digest\"]\n        3d[\"3d: Check duplicate\"]\n        3e[\"3e: Insert blob\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Migration[\"Auto-Migration System\"]\n        5a[\"5a: Check source dir\"]\n        5b[\"5b: Verify metadata\"]\n        5c[\"5c: Execute migration\"]\n        5d[\"5d: Read from source\"]\n        5e[\"5e: Write to dest\"]\n        5f[\"5f: Preserve pins\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph OutputHandling[\"Output Truncation \u0026 Policy\"]\n        4a[\"4a: Enforce limit\"]\n        4b[\"4b: Check CAS policy\"]\n        4c[\"4c: Store in CAS\"]\n        4d[\"4d: Build wrapper\"]\n        4e[\"4e: Apply policy\"]\n        4f[\"4f: Hint branch\"]\n        4g[\"4g: Generate commands\"]\n    end\n\n    Config --\u003e|provides driver and policy| Factory\n    Factory --\u003e|selects file backend| FileStore\n    Factory --\u003e|selects db backend| DBAbstraction\n    DBAbstraction --\u003e|creates| DBStores\n    Factory --\u003e|triggers after store creation| Migration\n    \n    Migration --\u003e|reads legacy objects| FileStore\n    Migration --\u003e|writes to new backend| DBStores\n    \n    Config --\u003e|provides expose policy| OutputHandling\n    OutputHandling --\u003e|respects store setting| Factory\n    OutputHandling --\u003e|stores large output| DBStores\n    \n    DBAbstraction --\u003e|abstracts sqlite/libsql/turso| DBStores\n\n    style Config fill:#fcc2d7\n    style Factory fill:#a5d8ff\n    style FileStore fill:#b2f2bb\n    style DBAbstraction fill:#d0bfff\n    style DBStores fill:#b2f2bb\n    style Migration fill:#ffec99\n    style OutputHandling fill:#ffec99"
}